WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.637
NARRATOR: In a remote
atoll near Tahiti,

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:09.075
Kori Garza, Andy Casagrande,
and safety diver [inaudible]

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.378
put themselves in
the line of fire.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.116
These investigators
test the theory

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:20.487
that some tiger sharks may work
together and hunt in packs.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.493
Before they know
it, they're fending

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:31.865
off a double approach by two
large tiger sharks, and more.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:48.815
Again and again, the sharks
seem to come in waves.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:00.894
It's too much.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:01.928
They must retreat.

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.604
ANDY CASAGRANDE: Hello.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.505
That was--

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.406
That was intense.

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.741
That was intense.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:19.045
I mean, there were pretty
insane moments on that camera.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.490
ANDY CASAGRANDE: I saw you
deflecting one coming here,

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.624
another one behind you.

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.993
And then at one point
you appeared literally

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.497
like dancing on tigers.

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:38.865
It was crazy, huh?

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:43.169
KORI GARZA: You see what I
mean, how they all disappeared?

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.004
And then instead of
just like one coming in,

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.172
it's boom, all at once.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:58.852
Here we go, 360 tiger sharks.

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:01.855
NARRATOR: They review the
footage and search for clues.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.123
If these tigers
cooperatively hunt,

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:07.527
it may suggest that great
whites could also do the same.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.498
KORI GARZA: Look at that.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.565
ANDY CASAGRANDE: Oh, wow.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.334
KORI GARZA: Oh, wow.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.235
Oh, there are--

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.202
ANDY CASAGRANDE: One, two.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.270
KORI GARZA: --three tigers.

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.204
ANDY CASAGRANDE: There's
three right there.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.439
And that other tiger--

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.440
KORI GARZA: Just keeps
following, swimming around.

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:21.941
ANDY CASAGRANDE:
Following that tiger.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.676
KORI GARZA: Yeah, he's
following that one.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.078
They come in in a fleet.

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:28.848
NARRATOR: After careful review,
Kori is convinced, tiger sharks

00:02:28.915 --> 00:02:31.284
working together makes sense.

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.052
KORI GARZA: It's better
for them and easier

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.754
for them to learn
to cooperate, rather

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:37.056
than to spend their whole
time fighting each other.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.658
NARRATOR: It could
be an anomaly,

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:42.328
unique to this species,
except for emerging

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:45.231
evidence from around the world.

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:50.136
From sand tiger sharks
off South Africa

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:56.276
to lemon sharks in Australia,
and gray reefs in French

00:02:56.342 --> 00:03:01.080
Polynesia, they've
all been observed

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:04.350
to seemingly work together.

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:09.155
And now this for the
tigers of Tahiti.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.557
ANDY CASAGRANDE:
This 360 shows us

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:12.825
that all of the
sharks in mass are

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:15.228
showing up together
and leaving together,

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:16.829
pretty much every single time.

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:17.864
KORI GARZA: Every single time.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:18.932
It's not, and this
is not coincidence.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.133
ANDY CASAGRANDE: This
isn't coincidence.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:21.968
Yeah, because it's
happening every single time.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.370
[bubbles]

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.473
[music playing]

